1
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,260
Why do any of them care?

2
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:12,700
I deserve to die like this.

3
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:16,393
Why can't they see I'm not
worth risking their lives for?

4
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:25,077
We, the second division of the Whitebeard
Pirates, will save our commander,

5
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:27,240
Ace, no matter what the cost. Yeah!

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,917
Please don't do this.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,200
Just stop.

8
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:33,800
Just let me die like I'm supposed to.

9
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:36,730
Ace!

10
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,700
You're my brother!

11
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,760
You can't be this stupid.

12
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:45,120
Stop, Luffy.

13
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:47,100
Turn around, Bobbs.

14
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,520
What is it, Ace?

15
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:10,620
I'm ready.

16
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:16,040
Ready to accept whatever I deserve.

17
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:20,140
I'll accept any help that's offered to me.

18
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:25,000
But I'll also accept any punishment.

19
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:33,960
Either one, whichever comes first.

20
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:41,620
I'm just ready for all this to end.

21
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:14,117
Every time the rain no longer falls.

22
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,317
And I see the sky.

23
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:19,257
I think back to when I was a child.

24
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,937
Who could only cry.

25
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:24,497
Blindly chasing after him.

26
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:29,317
I fall far behind my only thought.

27
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:32,397
One day I will be stronger.

28
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:37,517
Grattery and gratitude
fading with the wind.

29
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,337
Am I stronger now than I was before?

30
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:42,420
Or as weak as back then?

31
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:45,637
I don't know for sure, but until I do.

32
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:48,157
My voyage will not end.

33
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,297
No matter what's next.

34
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:53,257
I'm walking straight ahead.

35
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:55,797
So let's go.

36
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:59,557
There's nothing that can stop us now.

37
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,857
Though time's not on our side.

38
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:04,477
We'll never let it pull us down.

39
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,637
And we may fall.

40
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:09,557
But we'll always keep on standing.

41
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:12,237
There's no way anything.

42
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:15,717
Will take what I hold dear away from me.

43
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:18,237
The voices inside me.

44
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:20,677
Push me to keep surviving.

45
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:23,557
I'll go on, I'll get through.

46
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:26,257
No matter what I gotta do.

47
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:30,177
The fiercest thoughts
of all can pour upon me.

48
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:35,320
I don't care why in the
world would I turn back.

49
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:41,277
So let's go.

50
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:44,897
There's nothing that can stop us now.

51
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:46,957
Though time's not on us.

52
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,837
I will never let it pull us down.

53
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:54,897
We may fall, but we'll
always keep on standing.

54
00:03:54,980 --> 00:04:01,097
There's no way everything will
take what I hold dear away from me.

55
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,860
I know the future's there for us to see.

56
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,417
Look at that punk.

57
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,217
It's like he's trying to steal the show.

58
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:26,657
Like this is his war.

59
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:28,637
It should be captain. Fuggies.

60
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,357
I think it's time, boss.

61
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:32,957
You gotta stand up and
show the world who you are.

62
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,257
This is the perfect.

63
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:36,237
Moment for you to defeat Whitebeard.

64
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:37,337
Maybe I will.

65
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:38,717
Maybe I will.

66
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:43,737
I gotta keep stalling.

67
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:44,777
This war is.

68
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:46,057
Completely bonkers.

69
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:48,757
It's nothing but monsters on both sides.

70
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:51,597
I'll just keep my head
down and stay. Quiet.

71
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,477
Hey, you clown nose.

72
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:56,117
What the hell did you just say to me?

73
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:58,940
Are you cruising for a bruising, punk?

74
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,777
I take it back.

75
00:05:04,860 --> 00:05:07,737
I thought I recognized you.

76
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:11,017
You worked for Roger back
when you were just a brat.

77
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:14,697
It's been a while, but it doesn't look
like things have changed too much.

78
00:05:14,780 --> 00:05:16,797
I can't believe I just threatened him.

79
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:18,157
He's gonna kill me.

80
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:19,977
Yep, he's a dead man.

81
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:21,697
His only chance is to run.

82
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:23,577
Holy crap, it's Whitebeard.

83
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:25,117
And he's speaking to him.

84
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:27,817
That is like the coolest
thing I've ever seen.

85
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:31,371
It's just further proof that
you're a genuine living lover.

86
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:33,920
Don't they realize I'm about to die?

87
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,917
Must be nice if it's not
your ass on the line?

88
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,720
You've got an entire
battalion of prisoners.

89
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:43,740
Now you're not planning on
challenging me, are you?

90
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:45,360
Yeah, we meet at last.

91
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:46,740
Now prepare yourself.

92
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:53,632
Jeez, he's pushing his luck
right off the edge of a cliff.

93
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:58,240
Oh yeah, it doesn't bother me
if you're hungry for a fight.

94
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:00,600
But if you beat me, then what's next?

95
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:04,729
Might be more Navy soldiers
than you can handle on your own.

96
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:08,977
Ah hell, if I'm being honest,
they're more than I can handle.

97
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:11,777
Now, I'm not one to back
down from a challenge,

98
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:14,597
but it would make more
sense to form an alliance.

99
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:17,480
Once we're done, then you can kick my ass!

100
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:19,937
Oh, holy crap!

101
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:23,440
Whitebeard actually recognizes
you as his brother-in-arms!

102
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:25,520
He considers you an equal!

103
00:06:25,780 --> 00:06:28,540
No, he called him a brat
like one minute ago!

104
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:30,857
Don't tell me you're gonna
try to take on the Navy!

105
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:33,469
You don't really think
you can win, do you?

106
00:06:34,220 --> 00:06:36,980
Well, yeah, I've just gotta go all out

107
00:06:38,140 --> 00:06:41,460
He's completely lost his
grip on reality! Seriously?

108
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:43,272
Oh, I've got goosebumps!

109
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:44,790
You know what?

110
00:06:44,873 --> 00:06:46,220
Maybe I can do this!

111
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:50,499
Maybe I really was destined to be
king, standing on top of the world!

112
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:53,957
I think you might be onto something.

113
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:56,452
Let's join forces and take down the Navy.

114
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:58,840
This is amazing!

115
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:00,520
Man, it's too much!

116
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:02,317
Alright, you win, Whitebeard.

117
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:05,197
I'll partner with you, but only
because you're begging me to.

118
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:06,160
Huh?

119
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,720
So arrogant!

120
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:10,600
Oh well, that's Captain Bobby!

121
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:14,081
Well, that guy is unbelievably
easy to manipulate.

122
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:16,680
He's a fool, to say the least.

123
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:20,077
But the prisoners he's got behind
him are something else entirely.

124
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,689
The last thing we need
now is more enemies.

125
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:27,840
Now, back to the war.

126
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,600
It's too late now!

127
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:34,292
They can't stop us from charging the bay!

128
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:35,210
Right!

129
00:07:35,293 --> 00:07:38,884
Now's our chance to finally join
Pops at the center of the fight!

130
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,550
Click.

131
00:07:41,633 --> 00:07:43,017
Come in, this is Whitebeard.

132
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:44,806
Put Squared on the line, now.

133
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:45,760
Oh, Pops!

134
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:47,511
You need Captain Squared?

135
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:51,637
Well, he, um, he was right here just
a few moments ago, but now, uh...

136
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,637
The thing is, I'm not
seeing him anywhere, sir!

137
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,661
Yeah, go figure.

138
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:59,469
All that tough talk, and then he's not
even around when you ask for his help.

139
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:00,390
Hmm.

140
00:08:00,473 --> 00:08:01,303
Well, so it goes.

141
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,459
Get me the DeKalvin Brothers, then.

142
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:05,140
Hey, Pops, what's up?

143
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:06,940
Yeah, Pops, what's up?

144
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,826
I want you to follow my lead.

145
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:11,784
Take command of all pirate
divisions around you.

146
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:13,590
Really?

147
00:08:13,673 --> 00:08:14,657
That's straight from Pops?

148
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:15,837
Well, all right, then.

149
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,449
I can take the right side.

150
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:18,857
I got it.

151
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:20,411
We'll take the left side.

152
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,780
Right. Understood.

153
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,016
We'll join in on the right side, too.

154
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:27,680
Okay, if that's what Pops wants.

155
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:30,024
My ship can take any direction.

156
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:31,356
Whatever works best.

157
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,077
Swart's missing.

158
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:34,737
No, I haven't seen him lately.

159
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:35,650
How unusual.

160
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:37,740
Sure thing.

161
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:39,549
We'll take the left flank.

162
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:42,997
Excuse me, Fleet Admiral, sir.

163
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:45,637
But the Pirates of the New World
have altered their battle tactics.

164
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:48,544
Yes, but it seems they've
turned to their sides.

165
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:52,351
They suddenly started attacking
the approaching Navy ships.

166
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:08,300
Your bluff's been called.

167
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:10,997
Whitebeard must have
sensed something's wrong.

168
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:14,080
So I tried a cheap trick
and he didn't fall for it.

169
00:09:14,260 --> 00:09:16,377
I'll admit it was a bit too obvious.

170
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:20,940
But still, he can't prevent the
inevitable just because he sees it coming.

171
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:25,970
Death!

172
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:27,040
Wee-haw!

173
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:28,877
Yee-haw!

174
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:31,320
Whoa, Eva, you're all right.

175
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:36,500
Eva, we've got to clear these
jerks out to get to Ace. Jeep it!

176
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,760
Fish mine karate. Yeah?

177
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:42,960
And Gum-Gum!

178
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:47,260
Five thousand brick fish. Wee!

179
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:48,630
Fasuka!

180
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:54,580
On we go!

181
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:02,257
Ah, Straw Hat, you don't really
think you can get past me.

182
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:03,170
Him again?

183
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:05,319
I shall be your opponent this time.

184
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,057
What are you talking about?

185
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:11,060
My karate skills will be more
than adequate to thwart you alone.

186
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:13,557
That's a mighty fine speech.

187
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:15,180
I'm impressed. Yes.

188
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:20,560
But that's good, because once I take care
of you, my zombies can run wild again.

189
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:22,217
You keep moving, Luffy.

190
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:24,297
Don't waste a moment on this villain.

191
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:25,210
I won't.

192
00:10:25,293 --> 00:10:26,123
Thanks a lot, Jinbei.

193
00:10:26,206 --> 00:10:29,420
Oh, man, I liked it better
when Jinbei was on our side.

194
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:32,140
It's my shadow.

195
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:38,280
Now, suffer damnation, Navy soldiers.

196
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,819
For your shadow shall fight for me.

197
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:53,115
You'll see how smug you are
when I turn you into sushi.

198
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:02,561
And I'm going to add your
shadow to my collection.

199
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:09,217
You'll spend the rest of your
life toiling within my darkness.

200
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:10,540
How does that sound?

201
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:14,000
I'll take that shadow now.

202
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:27,480
FISHMAN CORROTTALE!

203
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,980
Sharkskin bob for us!

204
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,960
And shark brick fist!

205
00:11:56,700 --> 00:12:00,537
In the end you gave up those coveted
shadows of yours rather easily.

206
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:02,697
Perhaps you should train yourself more.

207
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:05,177
It's time you gave up and let me pass.

208
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:06,317
I'm done with you.

209
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:08,017
My only concern is ace.

210
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,597
You don't get to lecture me.

211
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:11,180
This fun's not over?

212
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,620
That's Straw Hat!

213
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:30,660
Move to Shiki!

214
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:38,600
Jeez!

215
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:39,970
It's you!

216
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:41,060
Smokey!

217
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:42,860
I finally found you.

218
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,600
About time. Oh, yeah.

219
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:48,782
I forgot this weapon is tipped
with sea prism stone, that cheater.

220
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:51,240
Fine. Second gear.

221
00:12:52,540 --> 00:12:55,180
I'm not going to let
you get away this time.

222
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:57,060
Come, come.

223
00:12:58,040 --> 00:12:58,870
Check.

224
00:12:59,060 --> 00:12:59,890
Got me!

225
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,400
White launcher!

226
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:08,100
You're a lot stronger than you used to be.

227
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:09,330
You're strong.

228
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:12,410
He's vanished!

229
00:13:12,493 --> 00:13:13,360
He's fast.

230
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,500
Where is he?

231
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:30,120
Seems I can return the compliment.

232
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:32,733
You're a real force to be reckoned with.

233
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:44,917
Hate to tell you, though, you're
still not strong enough to beat me.

234
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,280
You cheap jerk! Move that thing!

235
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:50,459
After all this time, I
finally understand the truth.

236
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:53,960
I know why Dragon really helped you.

237
00:13:54,180 --> 00:13:56,886
If it weren't for him
that day, you'd be dead.

238
00:13:57,980 --> 00:14:02,960
You may have had Dragon to save you in
Loguetown, but no one's gonna save you today.

239
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:05,080
This sucks.

240
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,125
Get your filthy hands off him!

241
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:11,720
My body's smoke, how'd she hit me?

242
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:15,080
You can't just kick him,
he ate a loggia fruit!

243
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:20,191
Wait a sec, why did the pirate
empress just save Straw Hat?

244
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,680
Hey Hancock, what the
hell's wrong with you?

245
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:26,977
Don't tell me you're resigning
from the warlords Shut your mouth!

246
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:31,057
The screaming fury in my heart has
rendered me deaf to your words How

247
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:34,797
dare you pin my beloved down with
your boorish club and threaten him?

248
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:38,380
You will die for your actions.

249
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:41,667
I've never felt this
angry in my entire life.

250
00:14:42,140 --> 00:14:45,500
I'll feed you piece by
piece to wild animals.

251
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,861
The Kucha's Haki is overwhelming.

252
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,260
Thanks, Hancock.

253
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:54,820
Of course.

254
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:57,948
Also, I'm happy you got
my name right again.

255
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:02,380
Please, listen. That's enough.

256
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:07,697
Kuma look it's me have
you forgotten my face if

257
00:15:07,780 --> 00:15:10,657
you don't stop friendship
be damned i will fight!

258
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:14,637
Back i don't know what
kind of a history you

259
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:18,197
two have but it doesn't
matter trust me Empire!

260
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:20,757
Ivankov there's really
no use in talking to

261
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:24,337
him as he is now
doflamingo what do you say?

262
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:27,037
Is something wrong with
him you're clearly a

263
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:29,797
friend of bartholomew
kuma's so i doubt you'll

264
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:33,157
take this well the man
you knew as the tyrant

265
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:35,840
kuma is not the man you see before you now

266
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:41,840
because that man is dead
but that can't be true!

267
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:51,420
How can kuma be dead?

268
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:59,640
What the hell just happened?

269
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:02,802
I thought Hancock was
supposed to be on our side?

270
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:10,540
Take this!

271
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:14,592
It's the key to your brother's handcuffs.

272
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,557
The touch of his hands.

273
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,257
They're strong.

274
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:25,620
Yet so kind.

275
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:27,610
Hancock.

276
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:29,290
Yay!

277
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:30,890
You're so awesome.

278
00:16:30,973 --> 00:16:31,937
I can hug you forever!

279
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:33,257
I'll never forget this.?

280
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:34,170
What a pal!

281
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:41,877
Oh, um, well?

282
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,477
It's really no trouble at all.

283
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:45,157
I'm just glad I could help out.

284
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:46,577
Never mind me, though, Lupi.

285
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:47,895
Just go and save Ace.

286
00:16:48,020 --> 00:16:48,961
Oh, yeah, right.

287
00:16:50,060 --> 00:16:50,920
Thanks again!

288
00:16:58,940 --> 00:16:59,770
No way!

289
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:02,880
He managed to defeat the
pirate empress! Unreal!

290
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:04,337
The stare did nothing.

291
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:05,480
He's a beast!

292
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:07,737
This is...

293
00:17:07,820 --> 00:17:10,277
what people call...

294
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:12,600
what they call marriage.

295
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:32,510
Yeah.

296
00:17:32,593 --> 00:17:33,423
Stay back, you fool!

297
00:17:33,506 --> 00:17:35,397
You shall not pass on my watch.

298
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:38,577
Geez, the Empress is
really looking down on him!

299
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:40,117
Looking down so far?

300
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,840
She started looking up.

301
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,609
Get out of my way, pirate.

302
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:46,237
You know what happens to
people who betray the Navy?

303
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:47,496
Well, do you, woman?

304
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:51,060
I'll do whatever I like,
and you will allow it.

305
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:54,640
Because I'm beautiful.

306
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,620
It's the exact thing I need.

307
00:17:59,220 --> 00:18:00,050
Impossible!

308
00:18:00,340 --> 00:18:01,400
Kuma is dead?

309
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:04,540
Then who's that big guy
standing behind you?

310
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:06,117
Stop spouting nonsense.

311
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,920
You can't deceive me.

312
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,350
It's Eva.

313
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:13,840
And that big guy from before!

314
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:25,669
So, uh, were you guys
friends or something?

315
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:28,820
We were, but he's not acting like himself.

316
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:35,080
I'm sure this is a lovely
trip down memory lane for you,

317
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:38,617
but I'm afraid the Kuma you
know is no longer with us.

318
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:43,417
This is the new model new
model what do you think

319
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:45,957
he's talking about he
wants to get under my skin?

320
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:49,257
Yeah okay he's acting
pretty different than usual

321
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:53,420
right now but he's still
kuma wake up buddy hey!

322
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:57,157
Are you deaf or just stupid?

323
00:18:57,240 --> 00:19:00,037
Trust me it's no use
trying to talk to him!

324
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:02,360
It happened just a few days.

325
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:04,480
ago. Dr.

326
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:09,307
Vegapunk, the government scientist,
finally finished his modifications on Kuma.

327
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:14,337
Now he's the ruthless weapon of death
he should have been from the start.

328
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:18,440
Ladies and gentlemen, the
former Bartholomew Kuma.

329
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:20,957
Doc Vegapunk? Mods?

330
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,097
What the hell are you talking about?

331
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:25,937
Kuma here volunteered
to be a guinea pig in

332
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:28,549
a study to build the
ultimate human weapon,

333
00:19:28,760 --> 00:19:30,920
run by the government, of course.

334
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:35,620
First, they modified his
hands, then his legs.

335
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:37,797
Although his mind was still intact,

336
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,557
they modified his body
piece by piece until he

337
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:43,346
was no longer the same
Kuma you know and love.

338
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:46,220
But that's nonsense!

339
00:19:46,660 --> 00:19:49,189
Kuma always hated the
government, you jerk!

340
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:52,637
As if he'd ever sacrifice
himself for their stupid plan!

341
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:53,600
Hey, Kuma!

342
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:54,740
Snap out of it!

343
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:55,780
It's me!

344
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,617
Stop yelling.

345
00:19:57,700 --> 00:19:59,557
It's starting to get on my nerves.

346
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:02,797
I don't know what kind of deal
he had with the government.

347
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:05,040
He was just fine a few days ago.

348
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:08,020
It's funny, but tragic.

349
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:10,479
Before you know it, someone's gone.

350
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:13,440
In Kuma's case,

351
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:18,405
he doesn't even realize he was ever human,
so the poor sap might as well be dead.

352
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:23,461
Now he's just a monster who the
government has do their dirty work.

353
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:31,380
It's the latest, the greatest, PASSA
FISTA, Pucci, your new old friend.

354
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:46,120
Kuma, what's the big idea?

355
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:49,713
You better stop shooting that
laser crap at me right now!

356
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:51,840
Yeah, I remember.

357
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:55,540
We will never meet again.

358
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:58,410
Farewell.

359
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,020
Even then, he knew.

360
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:02,740
What's wrong, Kuma?

361
00:21:02,940 --> 00:21:04,640
Surely you recognize me?

362
00:21:05,460 --> 00:21:07,800
That was spooky. Now where is he?

363
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:15,280
Hey, watch out, you guys! Get away!

364
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:18,560
Pad cannon.

365
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:33,060
Damn it, Kuma!

366
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:34,360
That's enough!

367
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:37,660
You forgot me!

368
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:40,240
But how about my face spectrum?

369
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:47,320
This ring a bell?

370
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:52,000
How about this?

371
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,420
Galaxy wing!

372
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:17,260
Oh, how dare you attack my sweet,
succulent crew of candy boys? You can!

373
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:21,580
I don't take unfashionable gestures
lightly, you conniving minks!

374
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:24,180
Vengeful care!

375
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:37,000
I have met a lot of people,

376
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:42,460
but no one forgets my face!

377
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:45,817
No one has ever forgotten
my face in my entire life!

378
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:47,606
This manga is damn favorable!

379
00:22:51,280 --> 00:22:52,110
Kuma!

380
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:55,577
If you want to forget who you
are, that's your business.

381
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:59,660
But if you can't remember how
dangerous the great Ivankov is,

382
00:22:59,860 --> 00:23:02,340
then I will beat it into you!

383
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:05,020
So get ready, hon!

384
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:08,900
He is pissed.

385
00:23:09,460 --> 00:23:10,820
I'll take it from here.

386
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:15,157
All right, my battling beauties, keep
going and back Straw Boy up, okay?

387
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:16,070
Roger!

388
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:19,720
Okay, Straw Boy, let's get him.

389
00:23:20,380 --> 00:23:21,720
Thanks, good luck!

390
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:24,660
Come on, ladies, get to the scaffold!

391
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:30,850
Ah!

392
00:23:30,933 --> 00:23:32,716
Starhat's gonna steal all my thunder!

393
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:37,000
Now commence Operation Ming, Captain
Buggy, the king of the pirates!

394
00:23:37,300 --> 00:23:39,947
Anything that's possible
with me at the helm!

395
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:44,417
The whole world will be taking it
back with my onslaught of awesomeness!

396
00:23:44,500 --> 00:23:46,937
All of you, follow my lead
and don't mess anything up!

397
00:23:47,020 --> 00:23:48,820
Forward, you fools! Ah!

398
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:54,700
I question the efficacy
of your latest strategy!

399
00:24:03,180 --> 00:24:04,360
They're too many.

400
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:10,860
I won't reach him like this.

401
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:14,797
Don't you even dream of touching our pops?

402
00:24:14,880 --> 00:24:16,320
Get out of my way.

403
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:23,580
What a pain in the ass.

404
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:26,112
He's going to mess up our rescue mission.

405
00:24:26,660 --> 00:24:28,320
I call this brilliant punk!

406
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:43,560
He's fast. Too fast.

407
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:44,980
And strong.

408
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,880
Quite a combination for someone that size.

409
00:25:00,220 --> 00:25:03,460
Congrats on your escape
from prison, Katorea Boy.

410
00:25:05,060 --> 00:25:08,580
So, did you enjoy the pool
of blood during your stay?

411
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:13,980
Doflamingo, keep out
of my business or else.

412
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:15,500
It's not your concern.

413
00:25:15,940 --> 00:25:17,640
Just making small talk.

414
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:21,240
So, listen, I think we
might make a good team.

415
00:25:24,300 --> 00:25:25,500
Stop right there!

416
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:27,200
Yeah, you missed!

417
00:25:27,800 --> 00:25:29,094
Half clear, Straw Hat!

418
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:31,660
Nice one!

419
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:46,080
Apologies, Shanks.

420
00:25:48,720 --> 00:25:51,400
But I will not hold back against him.

421
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:55,480
Hey, I know him!

422
00:26:06,100 --> 00:26:09,020
I wonder what is written.

423
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:12,260
Will my hand wipe his name from history?

424
00:26:13,080 --> 00:26:20,000
Or perhaps his fortune shall spare him
the fury of this black sword I wield.
